course: dictionary
lesson: 3699
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word flatten can mean to press something flat, to knock something down, or to become flat. «Ears turned back or flattened mean a cat is scared or angry.» Here flattened means pressed down flat against the head, because that is what a frightened cat's ears do.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence to check it. In «The storm flattened the trees», flattened cannot mean pressed flat with a rolling pin, because trees are not pressed. The storm knocked them down, so the meaning is destroyed or knocked down completely.
explain: Look for phrases too. «The hills flatten out near the sea» uses flatten out, which means the land becomes level and flat. Flatten out is a clue: when you see out after a word, the phrase often means something is changing into a new state.
fact: Flatten means to make something flat or flatter by pressing or rolling it.
fact: Flatten can also mean to knock down or destroy something completely, as in «The storm flattened the trees».
fact: Flatten out means to become flat, as in «The hills flatten out near the sea».
fact: Cooks flatten dough with a rolling pin, and people flatten a cardboard box before they put it in the bin.
exercise: «Small raindrops are round, and bigger ones are flattened at the bottom like a burger bun as they fall.» What does flattened mean here? | *Pressed or squashed into a flatter shape | Blown high into the sky | Turned into a teardrop | Made into a shiny ball
exercise: «Ears turned back or flattened mean a cat is scared or angry.» What does flattened mean? | Pointed up high | Covered in fur | Cut off | *Pressed down flat against the head
exercise: «After dinner you rinse a tin, flatten a cereal box and drop a bottle into the right bin.» What does flatten mean here? | Fill it with water | *Press it down so it lies flat | Throw it away whole | Paint it bright colours
test: «The hills flatten out near the sea.» What does flatten out mean? | The hills shout loudly | The hills sink under the water | The hills grow taller | *The land becomes flat and level
test: «The storm flattened the trees.» Which meaning fits best? | Watered them slowly | *Knocked them down completely | Painted them green | Counted them one by one
exam: «It is impossible to flatten the surface of a sphere onto paper without stretching, squashing or tearing it.» Which meaning of flatten fits here? | Knock something down completely | Cook something until it is soft | Become flat over time | *Make something flat by pressing or rolling it
